text:
PROSE:
Rhea gripped the Null-Value Token in her left hand, its heavy, light-swallowing edges biting into her skin as they left the jagged outskirts behind. They dragged their battered bodies up the final incline, stopping dead at the polished marble steps of the sanctum entrance. Two towering, gold-plated guards stood at the threshold, their featureless visors tracking the party's arrival with mechanical indifference.

[Stamina: 1/150]
[Status Effect: Exhaustion (Severe) - Movement speed and physical actions severely penalized.]

Every breath Rhea took felt like she was inhaling powdered glass. She leaned heavily against a basalt pillar, the rough stone scraping against her singed arm hair. The token pulsed in her grip, a localized glitch in reality. Having just crafted the Null-Value Token out of sheer desperation and the last of their refunded materials, she knew this was their only shot. They had already discovered the overseer's budget was finite, tied to the local mana ledger, but finite didn't mean small. He could still afford to execute them.

Beside her, Vance tightened his grip on his rusted Rebar. His heavily blistered hands bled sluggishly over the iron, the skin weeping from the burns he'd suffered in the maintenance trenches. He looked like a man who had already died twice and was simply waiting for the paperwork to clear.

[HP: 10/150]
[Status Effect: Audit Compliance (Red-Tier) - Lethal force authorized by local administration.]

"I step up, they look at me," Vance muttered, his voice a dry rasp. "You do the math and throw that thing."

Behind them, Unit 734 let out a metallic, rattling wheeze. Plumes of thick gray exhaust vented continuously from its smoking chassis, the drone struggling to maintain a stable hover. 

[Chassis Integrity: 34%]
[Warning: Critical System Failure Imminent.]

"Just keep them focused on you," Rhea said, her voice shaking but her grip on the token absolute. "If they scan my inventory before I trigger the exploit, the node will delete us both."

The elite bureaucratic guards were perfectly symmetrical, their gold-plated armor etched with scrolling ledgers of System law. They held massive halberds that hummed with administrative violence. They didn't breathe. They didn't blink. They merely waited for a violation.

Vance didn't hesitate. He rolled his shoulders, stepped out from behind the pillar, and slammed the Rebar against the pristine marble stairs. The sharp, metallic crack echoed across the courtyard, a profound insult to the sanctum's order.

Both guards snapped their featureless visors toward him in perfect unison.

[Aggro Generated: Vance Harrow.]
[Threat Assessment: Hostile. Initiating Deletion Protocol.]

The air pressure dropped as the guards raised their weapons, their targeting lasers painting a glowing red crosshair squarely on Vance's chest. He planted his feet at the threshold, drawing the entirety of their lethal focus, while Rhea stepped out from the shadows, raising the token for the final breach.

